#: processes/publish-verification.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the findings. `yes` (exit 0) ends verified and the caller deploys; `no` (exit 1) ends failed, and the caller blocks the deploy and alerts the publication manager with the report."
msgstr ""

#: processes/publish-verification.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the verifier set's exit code. `no` (exit 2 — nothing to verify, or a verifier could not run) ends as could-not-verify, which the caller treats as a failure: an unverified release is not a verified one. `yes` asks whether everything passed."
msgstr ""

#: processes/publish-verification.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Bean vigi, owner 2026-09-23: a set of post-processing tools that verify what the build produced, run BEFORE deployment and blocking — \"a failure triggers an alert to the publisher manager\". This process only verifies and says how it went; the caller (docs-site-publish) blocks the deploy on anything but a pass and routes the failure through Process_PublishAlert, the one alert every step after the publish button shares."
msgstr ""

